#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:10
msgid "The Test Class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:12
msgid ""
"In order to take advantage of the built-in database tools that "
"CodeIgniter provides for testing, your tests must extend "
"``CIUnitTestCase`` and use the ``DatabaseTestTrait``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:17
msgid ""
"Because special functionality executed during the ``setUp()`` and "
"``tearDown()`` phases, you must ensure that you call the parent's methods"
" if you need to use those methods, otherwise you will lose much of the "
"functionality described here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:24
msgid "Setting Up a Test Database"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:26
msgid ""
"When running database tests, you need to provide a database that can be "
"used during testing. Instead of using the PHPUnit built-in database "
"features, the framework provides tools specific to CodeIgniter. The first"
" step is to ensure that you have set up a ``tests`` database group in "
"**app/Config/Database.php**. This specifies a database connection that is"
" only used while running tests, to keep your other data safe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:31
msgid ""
"If you have multiple developers on your team, you will likely want to "
"keep your credentials stored in the **.env** file. To do so, edit the "
"file to ensure the following lines are present and have the correct "
"information::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:44
msgid "Migrations and Seeds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:46
msgid ""
"When running tests, you need to ensure that your database has the correct"
" schema set up and that it is in a known state for every test. You can "
"use migrations and seeds to set up your database, by adding a couple of "
"class properties to your test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:53
msgid "Migrations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:56
msgid "$migrate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:58
msgid ""
"This boolean value determines whether the database migration runs before "
"test. By default, the database is always migrated to the latest available"
" state as defined by ``$namespace``. If ``false``, migration never runs. "
"If you want to disable migration, set ``false``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:63
msgid "$migrateOnce"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:65
msgid ""
"This boolean value determines whether the database migration runs only "
"once. If you want to run migration once before the first test, set "
"``true``. If not present or ``false``, migration runs before each test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:70
msgid "$refresh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:72
msgid ""
"This boolean value determines whether the database is completely "
"refreshed before test. If ``true``, all migrations are rolled back to "
"version 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:76
msgid "$namespace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:78
msgid ""
"By default, CodeIgniter will look in "
"**tests/_support/Database/Migrations** to locate the migrations that it "
"should run during testing. You can change this location by specifying a "
"new namespace in the ``$namespace`` properties. This should not include "
"the **Database\\\\Migrations** sub-namespace but just the base namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:82
msgid ""
"If you set this property to ``null``, it runs migrations from all "
"available namespaces like ``php spark migrate --all``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:85
msgid "Seeds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:88
msgid "$seed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:90
msgid ""
"If present and not empty, this specifies the name of a Seed file that is "
"used to populate the database with test data prior to test running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:94
msgid "$seedOnce"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:96
msgid ""
"This boolean value determines whether the database seeding runs only "
"once. If you want to run database seeding once before the first test, set"
" ``true``. If not present or ``false``, database seeding runs before each"
" test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:101
msgid "$basePath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:103
msgid ""
"By default, CodeIgniter will look in **tests/_support/Database/Seeds** to"
" locate the seeds that it should run during testing. You can change this "
"directory by specifying the ``$basePath`` property. This should not "
"include the **Seeds** directory, but the path to the single directory "
"that holds the sub-directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:108
msgid "Helper Methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:110
msgid ""
"The **DatabaseTestTrait** class provides several helper methods to aid in"
" testing your database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:113
msgid "Changing Database State"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:116
msgid "regressDatabase()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:118
msgid ""
"Called during ``$refresh`` described above, this method is available if "
"you need to reset the database manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:121
msgid "migrateDatabase()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:123
msgid ""
"Called during ``setUp()``, this method is available if you need to run "
"migrations manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:126
msgid "seed($name)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:128
msgid ""
"Allows you to manually load a Seed into the database. The only parameter "
"is the name of the seed to run. The seed must be present within the path "
"specified in ``$basePath``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:132
msgid "hasInDatabase($table, $data)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:134
msgid ""
"Inserts a new row into the database. This row is removed after the "
"current test runs. ``$data`` is an associative array with the data to "
"insert into the table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:140
msgid "Getting Data from Database"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:143
msgid "grabFromDatabase($table, $column, $criteria)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:145
msgid ""
"Returns the value of ``$column`` from the specified table where the row "
"matches ``$criteria``. If more than one row is found, it will only return"
" the first one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:151
msgid "Assertions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:154
msgid "dontSeeInDatabase($table, $criteria)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:156
msgid ""
"Asserts that a row with criteria matching the key/value pairs in "
"``$criteria`` DOES NOT exist in the database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:161
msgid "seeInDatabase($table, $criteria)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:163
msgid ""
"Asserts that a row with criteria matching the key/value pairs in "
"``$criteria`` DOES exist in the database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:168
msgid "seeNumRecords($expected, $table, $criteria)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/database.rst:170
msgid ""
"Asserts that a number of matching rows are found in the database that "
"match ``$criteria``."
msgstr ""

